Z||000004||MrPBody||11-07-2000||11:48 PM||||I bought my Fiero because I didn't find the right bike.  I thought my friend John wanted to sell his old Yamaha RD350, but he decided to keep it.  You might try one of those; it's lightweight, simple, agile, and fast.  And one model year ('75, I think) was painted orange almost like your GT.  So what if they're 25 years old?  They're not easy to find, though.<P>And the '79 RD400 Daytona came stock with rearset pegs and fairing.<P>Maybe too old and perverse, but I like them.<BR>||||reg||1
